    "field": "Glacial biogeochemistry",
    "problem": "The causes for the substantial increase in atmospheric methane since the Last Glacial Maximum remain unclear, as models struggle to reconcile the observed concentration amplitude by simulating competing hypotheses of fluctuating methane sources versus changes in its atmospheric lifetime.",
    "method": "To understand the glacial methane cycle, this study uses an Earth System model with interactive chemistry and vegetation to comprehensively assess competing hypotheses by simulating changes in major natural methane sources and atmospheric lifetime between the Last Glacial Maximum and pre-industrial periods.",
    "task": "The task is to use an Earth System model to assess competing hypotheses about changes in methane sources and atmospheric lifetime to explain the observed difference in methane concentrations between the Last Glacial Maximum and the pre-industrial era.",
